Add opt-in project-private Vulkan queues while preserving SDL resource lifetime.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    The engine needs separate compute and transfer queue submissions on the same
    VkDevice and real SDL resources. Upstream SDL creates one unified queue and
    provides no public queue-selection or semaphore-dependency API. This private
    project extension is not submitted upstream. The tracked SDL submodule stays
    pristine; scripts/vendor-tree.sh applies this patch to an archived build copy.

BUILD AND ABI
    Compile the copied SDL target with ATOMIC_GPU_QUEUE_EXTENSION and private
    include paths for mono.build/private and SDL's src/video/khronos. Without the
    define, no private header is needed. Runtime opt-in defaults false. The
    versioned callback table in AtomicGpuQueues.h is obtained through existing
    SDL device-property exports, so no SDL dynapi or shared-library exports change.

SYNCHRONIZATION AND LIFETIME
    The extension requests graphics, dedicated compute and dedicated transfer
    families when available. Pools are keyed by acquiring thread and family.
    Bounded graph semaphores are copied into each SDL command buffer. All graph
    waits use ALL_COMMANDS in ABI v1. SDL submit, fence and reference cleanup remain
    authoritative. Concurrent sharing removes family ownership handoffs; ordinary
    image layouts and explicit graph data dependencies still apply. Resources must
    keep their active generation fixed throughout worker recording. An owner
    preparation signal covers SDL's implicit texture-initialization submissions.
    Recording batches exclude defragmentation; explicit maintenance drains queues
    before using SDL's existing compaction path. Empty maintenance does not wait.

VALIDATION
    An isolated headless RTX 4090 fixture passed ordinary opt-out and opt-in paths:
    transfer buffer/texture upload, semaphore handoff, actual compute dispatch,
    graphics download and exact byte parity. Local Khronos validation was enabled
    with synchronization checks and reported no diagnostics. This demonstrates
    correctness, not measured physical hardware overlap or recording speedup.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Pinned SDL commit: fa2c02bb6e21974a89ea9824bc53c9932abe5f9c.
    Re-point the common-header initializer, pool key, logical-device creation,
    allocation/barrier helpers, submission and callback publication hunks. Do not
    edit mono.vendor/sdl in place. The private header and patch budget constants
    are checked at compile time.

